d: Describe response types"></a><h3 id=3D"describe-response-types" class=3D=
"heading-anchor">Describe response types</h3></div>
<p>Developers consuming a web API are most concerned with what's returned=
=E2=80=94specifically response types and error codes (if not standard). The=
 response types and error codes are denoted in the XML comments and data an=
notations.</p>
<p>The <code>Create</code> action returns an HTTP 201 status code on succes=
s. An HTTP 400 status code is returned when the posted request body is null=
. Without proper documentation in the Swagger UI, the consumer lacks knowle=
dge of these expected outcomes. Fix that problem by adding the highlighted =
lines in the following example:</p>
