<mark>    app.UseSwagger();</mark>
<span>
    <span class=3D"hljs-comment">// Enable middleware to serve swagger-ui (=
HTML, JS, CSS, etc.)</span></span>
<mark>    app.UseSwaggerUI();</mark>
<span>
    app.UseRouting();
    app.UseEndpoints(endpoints =3D&gt;
    {
        endpoints.MapControllers();
    });
}
</span></code></pre>
<div class=3D"alert is-info">
<p class=3D"alert-title"><span class=3D"docon docon-status-error-outline" a=
ria-hidden=3D"true"></span> Note</p>
<p>Swashbuckle relies on MVC's <a href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us=
/dotnet/api/microsoft.aspnetcore.mvc.apiexplorer" class=3D"no-loc" data-lin=
ktype=3D"absolute-path">Microsoft.AspNetCore.Mvc.ApiExplorer</a> to discove=
r the routes and endpoints. If the project calls <a href=3D"https://learn.m=
icrosoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/microsoft.extensions.dependencyinjection.mvcs=
ervicecollectionextensions.addmvc" class=3D"no-loc" data-linktype=3D"absolu=
te-path">AddMvc</a>, routes and endpoints are discovered automatically. Whe=
n calling <a href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/microsoft=
.extensions.dependencyinjection.mvccoreservicecollectionextensions.addmvcco=
re" class=3D"no-loc" data-linktype=3D"absolute-path">AddMvcCore</a>, the <a=
 href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/dotnet/api/microsoft.extensions.=
dependencyinjection.mvcapiexplorermvccorebuilderextensions.addapiexplorer" =
class=3D"no-loc" data-linktype=3D"absolute-path">AddApiExplorer</a> method =
must be explicitly called. For more information, see <a href=3D"https://git=
hub.com/domaindrivendev/Swashbuckle.AspNetCore#swashbuckle-apiexplorer-and-=
routing" data-linktype=3D"external">Swashbuckle, ApiExplorer, and Routing</=
a>.</p>
</div>
<p>The preceding <code>UseSwaggerUI</code> method call enables the <a href=
=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/aspnet/core/fundamentals/static-files=
?view=3Daspnetcore-7.0" data-linktype=3D"relative-path">Static File Middlew=
are</a>. If targeting .NET Framework or .NET Core 1.x, add the <a href=3D"h=
ttps://www.nuget.org/packages/Microsoft.AspNetCore.StaticFiles/" data-linkt=
ype=3D"external">Microsoft.AspNetCore.StaticFiles</a> NuGet package to the =
project.</p>
<p>Launch the app, and navigate to <code>http://localhost:&lt;port&gt;/swag=
ger/v1/swagger.json</code>. The generated document describing the endpoints=
 appears as shown in <a href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/aspnet/co=
re/tutorials/web-api-help-pages-using-swagger?view=3Daspnetcore-7.0#openapi=
-specification-openapijson" data-linktype=3D"relative-path">OpenAPI specifi=
cation (openapi.json)</a>.</p>
<p>The Swagger UI can be found at <code>http://localhost:&lt;port&gt;/swagg=
er</code>. Explore the API via Swagger UI and incorporate it in other progr=
ams.</p>
<div class=3D"alert is-success">
<p class=3D"alert-title"><span class=3D"docon docon-lightbulb" aria-hidden=
=3D"true"></span> Tip</p>
<p>To serve the Swagger UI at the app's root (<code>http://localhost:&lt;po=
rt&gt;/</code>), set the <code>RoutePrefix</code> property to an empty stri=
ng:</p>
<div class=3D"codeHeader" id=3D"code-try-31" data-bi-name=3D"code-header"><=
span class=3D"language">C#</span>
		<button type=3D"button" class=3D"action position-relative display-none-pr=
int" data-bi-name=3D"copy">
