			<div class=3D"successful-copy-alert position-absolute right-0 top-0 left=
-0 bottom-0 display-flex align-items-center justify-content-center has-text=
-success-invert has-background-success is-transparent" aria-hidden=3D"true"=
>
				<span class=3D"icon font-size-lg">
					<span class=3D"docon docon-check-mark"></span>
				</span>
			</div>
		</button>
	</div><pre class=3D"has-inner-focus"><code class=3D"lang-csharp" highlight=
-lines=3D"4" data-author-content=3D"app.UseSwaggerUI(c =3D>
{
    c.SwaggerEndpoint(&quot;/swagger/v1/swagger.json&quot;, &quot;My API V1=
&quot;);
    c.RoutePrefix =3D string.Empty;
});
"><span>app.UseSwaggerUI(c =3D&gt;
{
    c.SwaggerEndpoint(<span class=3D"hljs-string">"/swagger/v1/swagger.json=
"</span>, <span class=3D"hljs-string">"My API V1"</span>);</span>
<mark>    c.RoutePrefix =3D <span class=3D"hljs-built_in">string</span>.Emp=
ty;</mark>
<span>});
</span></code></pre>
</div>
<p>If using directories with IIS or a reverse proxy, set the Swagger endpoi=
nt to a relative path using the <code>./</code> prefix. For example, <code>=
./swagger/v1/swagger.json</code>. Using <code>/swagger/v1/swagger.json</cod=
e> instructs the app to look for the JSON file at the true root of the URL =
(plus the route prefix, if used). For example, use <code>http://localhost:&=
lt;port&gt;/&lt;route_prefix&gt;/swagger/v1/swagger.json</code> instead of =
<code>http://localhost:&lt;port&gt;/&lt;virtual_directory&gt;/&lt;route_pre=
fix&gt;/swagger/v1/swagger.json</code>.</p>
<div class=3D"alert is-info">
<p class=3D"alert-title"><span class=3D"docon docon-status-error-outline" a=
ria-hidden=3D"true"></span> Note</p>
<p>By default, Swashbuckle generates and exposes Swagger JSON in version 3.=
0 of the specification=E2=80=94officially called the OpenAPI Specification.=
 To support backwards compatibility, you can opt into exposing JSON in the =
2.0 format instead. This 2.0 format is important for integrations such as M=
icrosoft Power Apps and Microsoft Flow that currently support OpenAPI versi=
on 2.0. To opt into the 2.0 format, set the <code>SerializeAsV2</code> prop=
erty in <code>Startup.Configure</code>:</p>
<div class=3D"codeHeader" id=3D"code-try-32" data-bi-name=3D"code-header"><=
span class=3D"language">C#</span>
		<button type=3D"button" class=3D"action position-relative display-none-pr=
int" data-bi-name=3D"copy">
			<span class=3D"icon margin-right-xxs" aria-hidden=3D"true">
				<span class=3D"docon docon-edit-copy"></span>
			</span>
			<span>Copy</span>
			<div class=3D"successful-copy-alert position-absolute right-0 top-0 left=
-0 bottom-0 display-flex align-items-center justify-content-center has-text=
-success-invert has-background-success is-transparent" aria-hidden=3D"true"=
>
				<span class=3D"icon font-size-lg">
					<span class=3D"docon docon-check-mark"></span>
				</span>
			</div>
		</button>
	</div><pre class=3D"has-inner-focus"><code class=3D"lang-csharp" highlight=
-lines=3D"4-7" data-author-content=3D"public void Configure(IApplicationBui=
lder app)
{
    // Enable middleware to serve generated Swagger as a JSON endpoint.
    app.UseSwagger(c =3D>
    {
        c.SerializeAsV2 =3D true;
    });

    // Enable middleware to serve swagger-ui (HTML, JS, CSS, etc.),
    // specifying the Swagger JSON endpoint.
    app.UseSwaggerUI(c =3D>
    {
        c.SwaggerEndpoint(&quot;/swagger/v1/swagger.json&quot;, &quot;My AP=
I V1&quot;);
