<p>The Swagger UI now clearly documents the expected HTTP response codes:</=
p>
<p><span class=3D"mx-imgBorder">
<img src=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/aspnet/core/tutorials/web-api=
-help-pages-using-swagger/_static/data-annotations-response-types.png?view=
=3Daspnetcore-7.0" alt=3D"Swagger UI showing POST Response Class descriptio=
n 'Returns the newly created Todo item' and '400 - If the item is null' for=
 status code and reason under Response Messages." data-linktype=3D"relative=
-path">
</span>
</p>
<p>In ASP.NET Core 2.2 or later, conventions can be used as an alternative =
to explicitly decorating individual actions with <code>[ProducesResponseTyp=
e]</code>. For more information, see <a href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com=
/en-us/aspnet/core/web-api/advanced/conventions?view=3Daspnetcore-7.0" data=
-linktype=3D"relative-path">Use web API conventions</a>.</p>
<p>To support the <code>[ProducesResponseType]</code> decoration, the <a hr=
ef=3D"https://github.com/domaindrivendev/Swashbuckle.AspNetCore/blob/master=
/README.md#swashbuckleaspnetcoreannotations" data-linktype=3D"external">Swa=
shbuckle.AspNetCore.Annotations</a> package offers extensions to enable and=
 enrich the response, schema, and parameter metadata.</p>
<div class=3D"heading-wrapper" data-heading-level=3D"h3"><a class=3D"anchor=
-link docon docon-link" href=3D"https://learn.microsoft.com/en-us/aspnet/co=
re/tutorials/getting-started-with-swashbuckle?view=3Daspnetcore-7.0&amp;tab=
s=3Dvisual-studio-code#customize-the-ui-1" aria-label=3D"Section titled: Cu=
stomize the UI"></a><h3 class=3D"heading-anchor" data-id=3D"customize-the-u=
i-1">Customize the UI</h3></div>
<p>The default UI is both functional and presentable. However, API document=
ation pages should represent your brand or theme. Branding the Swashbuckle =
components requires adding the resources to serve static files and building=
 the folder structure to host those files.</p>
<p>If targeting .NET Framework or .NET Core 1.x, add the <a href=3D"https:/=
/www.nuget.org/packages/Microsoft.AspNetCore.StaticFiles" data-linktype=3D"=
external">Microsoft.AspNetCore.StaticFiles</a> NuGet package to the project=
:</p>
<div class=3D"codeHeader" id=3D"code-try-51" data-bi-name=3D"code-header"><=
span class=3D"language">XML</span>
